WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.940 --> 00:00:04.060
Companion Experiences for Microsoft Teams Meetings.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.300
Video meetings traditionally limit each person to one device,

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.520
but many meeting tasks would be easier with two devices.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:15.060
Ann works at a table in a design studio with a Microsoft Surface Pro and mobile phone.

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:18.120
In Microsoft Teams you can use your devices together.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.430
Ann joins a Microsoft Teams video meeting on her Surface Pro.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:23.140
Bob and Cath are in the meeting.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.440
Ann joins her phone as a companion to her Surface Pro in the meeting.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.240
Use your computer and phone together to present live mobile video.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.540
Ann stands up and walks to a large 3D physical model of a pie chart.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:43.960
Ann stands in front of the physical pie
chart and selects "Share video" from her phone's Teams interface.

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:47.020
Ann sees a preview of the video of the physical pie chart.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.840
Ann presses "Start presenting" and the video from her phone can be seen

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.840
maximized on Bob and Cath's views of the meeting.

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.020
She moves around the model pointing at various parts.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.540
Use your computer and phone together to take and present photos.

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:04.900
Ann chooses "Share photo" from the menu.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:11.020
Ann gets ready to take a picture of colour guides pinned to the wall.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:13.580
She takes the photo and presses "Start
presenting."

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.640
Bob and Cath see the photo.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:21.120
She returns to her table, puts the phone down and talks about the photo.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.880
Use your computer and phone together to continue your meeting on the go.

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.560
Ann looks at her watch and tells Bob and Cath that she has to leave.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.660
Ann picks up her phone and turns on camera, microphone, and speaker.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:42.660
She talks to Bob and Cath as she shuts her Surface Pro and walks away.

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:50.860
Use your computer and phone together to
present your phone screen.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:55.300
The next day, Ann is in a lecture hall which is also a Teams meeting.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.160
Dave and Ed are watching remotely.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:02:02.140
On her phone, Ann starts the Edge web browser and scrolls down a web page.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:06.580
The computer shows a mirrored view, and Dave and Ed see the same view.

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:10.440
The lecture hall audience sees Ann walking around presenting her phone screen.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:14.280
Use your computer and phone together to
remote control PowerPoint.

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:18.620
In the lecture, Anne's phone and computer show a PowerPoint presentation.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.320
Dave and Ed see the same presentation.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:27.300
The lecture hall audience sees Ann walking around presenting her phone to remote control PowerPoint.

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.180
Presented by Microsoft.

